FFCapital is a new BootLoops program that reads the saved-state files written
by FireFly (https://gitlab.com/firefly-library/firefly; J. Klappert, S. Y.
Klein and F. Lange; Copyright (C) 2020 Jonas Klappert and Fabian Lange; GNU
General Public License v3.0 or later). The file layout was taken from
FireFly's source code. No FireFly routine is included or run, and FireFly
itself is not included.

Mixed licensing. harvest_ffsave_eta.py and harvest_ffsave_2var.py are
distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later
(LICENSE-GPL-3.0 beside this file), with the FireFly notice in their headers,
because they contain the list PRIMES: the first 40 entries of FireFly's table
of the largest 63-bit primes, copied from source/ReconstHelper.cpp (primes())
in its three-per-line layout. All three scripts, including the MIT-licensed
recon_symbolic_d.py, also hold the 24 section names of a state file in the
order in which FireFly's writer RatReconst::save_state
(source/RatReconst.cpp) emits them, and a reader of the state file written
from that writer. The two harvest scripts also hold a reader of the
validation.gz file written from source/include/firefly/Reconstructor.hpp.
Each of the two scripts is a stand-alone command-line program; nothing else
in this package imports them.

recon_symbolic_d.py and selftest.py are MIT-licensed. recon_symbolic_d.py
contains no prime table (it reads the primes at run time from the user's own
copy of FireFly's ReconstHelper.cpp, option --ff-helper); its tuple
STATE_SECTIONS holds the same 24 section names, taken from the same FireFly
writer, and its header says so. selftest.py generates its primes.

